---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE, TAGLINE } from '../config';
import Distribution from '../components/illus/Distribution.astro';
import LayoutMosaic from '../components/illus/LayoutMosaic.astro';
import RCalendar from '../components/illus/RCalendar.astro';
import CockpitMock from '../components/illus/CockpitMock.astro';
import PayoutLock from '../components/illus/PayoutLock.astro';
import DynamicRisk from '../components/illus/DynamicRisk.astro';
---
<Base bare>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">For prop traders · Windows app</p>
      {/* Die Überschrift führt mit dem Ergebnis, nicht mit dem Mittel (Michael 2026-08-29):
          „shows you risk" war eine Aussage darüber, was wir verweigern — eine
          Verkäufer-Tugend, keine Käufer-Sehnsucht.

          Die Grenze aus D0 Punkt 3 ist scharf und wurde einmal gerissen: „Calm is a
          setup. Not a character trait." war stark, aber FALSCH — Temperament gibt es,
          und der Satz sprach den Trader frei. Das ist der Guru-Zug spiegelverkehrt.
          Die jetzige Fassung behauptet deshalb nichts über den Trader, sondern über
          den BAU: „built to" ist Konstruktionsabsicht, keine Zusage. „Level" trägt
          zugleich die Flug-Metapher, die im Wort Cockpit ohnehin steckt (künstlicher
          Horizont) — s. Blogartikel „Fly by instruments".

          Die These steht weiter offensiv in der Unterzeile — sie ist nach D0 das
          Messinstrument der Positionierung und darf die Sichtfläche nicht verlassen. */}
      <h1>Everything on this screen is built to keep you level.</h1>
      {/* Michael 2026-08-29: der Kern ist NICHT „Risiko statt Geld" — 0,25 % ist genauso
          eine Risikozahl wie ein Betrag. Der Kern ist RELATIV statt ABSOLUT: die Zahl
          verschwindet nicht, sie wechselt die Skala und wird dadurch unvergleichbar mit
          dem eigenen Leben. Das ist `07` D0 Argument 2, das dort fälschlich als
          Nebenargument für Skeptiker geführt wurde — es ist der Wirkmechanismus.
          Das Notional-Argument („in dem Konto ist kein Geld") trägt weiter unten das
          eigene dunkle Band; hier wäre es eine Dopplung. */}
      <p class="lede">
        <strong>Same trader, better conditions.</strong> FixedR is a trading cockpit for funded
        accounts where the numbers don't disappear — they change scale. You risk
        0.5&thinsp;%, not an amount; a loss reads <span class="r-value">−1R</span>, not a sum
        you can hold against your rent.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/manifesto">Why no money?</a>
      </div>
      <p class="meta">
        Works with <strong>MetaTrader</strong> &amp; <strong>NinjaTrader</strong> ·
        runs on your machine · no cloud account
      </p>

      <div class="stage">
        <div class="bar">
          <i></i><i></i><i></i>
          <span>{SITE_TITLE} — {TAGLINE}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="body"><CockpitMock /></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Abgrenzung: was es ist -->
  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Not another journal</p>
        <h2>Most tools analyze the trade after it's gone.</h2>
        <p>
          FixedR sits where the decision happens. It places the order, sizes it from your risk,
          and records the whole thing on the way through — so the journal fills itself and the
          rules apply <em>before</em> the trade exists, not in the review afterwards.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="token">
            <span class="bars"><b></b><b></b><b></b></span>
            <span class="lbl">STOP · REQUIRED</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Mandatory stop-loss</h3>
          <p>No stop, no trade. Risk is fixed before entry — not renegotiated with yourself while the position runs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="token">
            <span class="lbl">RISK</span><span class="val brand">1 R</span>
            <span class="arrow">→</span>
            <span class="lbl">SIZE</span><span class="val">4.2</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Position size from risk</h3>
          <p>You set the risk, FixedR computes the size from your stop distance. Backwards from the usual — and the only sane direction.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          {/* Der Betrag ist bewusst unlesbar: die Karte behauptet, dass Geld außer
              Sicht bleibt — sie darf ihn nicht selbst wieder herstellen. */}
          <div class="token">
            <span class="val">+2.4 R</span>
            <span class="masked" aria-label="a currency amount, deliberately hidden">
              <span class="cur">$</span><i></i><i class="sep"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h3>Money stays out of sight</h3>
          <p>Results, targets, drawdown headroom — all in R. No money mode, no toggle. The absence is the feature.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Feature-Bänder -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for funded accounts</p>
        <h2>One trade, every account, one set of rules.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="illu-box"><Distribution /></div>
        <div>
          <h2>Distribute a trade across accounts</h2>
          <p>
            Trading several funded accounts means executing the same idea several times, by hand,
            under time pressure. In FixedR you place it once and it goes out by your configuration.
          </p>
          <p>
            And a hard promise: <strong>without configuration, nothing is guessed.</strong> An
            unconfigured account stops the distribution with a loud error instead of quietly
            doing something almost right.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-row flip">
        <div class="illu-box"><LayoutMosaic /></div>
        <div>
          <h2>Timeframes that stay in sync</h2>
          <p>
            Put the same symbol on several timeframes side by side, and give each chart a
            role — <span class="r-value">HTF</span>, <span class="r-value">MTF</span>,
            <span class="r-value">LTF</span>. The synchronisation follows the role, not the
            window.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is the difference between an arrangement of windows and a named analysis
            structure: the charts belong together because you said what each one is for.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-row">
        <div class="illu-box"><RCalendar /></div>
        <div>
          <h2>Your month in R</h2>
          <p>
            Because R is defined by your own risk, the record stays comparable across accounts,
            account sizes and years. Scale from a 10k account to a 100k and the calendar reads
            exactly the same — that's the point.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Mehrere Konten: der Blickwinkel, den nur eine übergreifende Anbindung hat -->
  <section class="alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">Several funded accounts</p>
        <h2>Your book is the unit. Not one account.</h2>
        <p>
          Risk tools live inside one platform: a NinjaTrader add-on guards NinjaTrader accounts,
          a MetaTrader script guards MetaTrader accounts, a firm's dashboard guards its own.
          FixedR connects all of them at once — so the rules can apply to the trader, not to
          a single login.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="illu"><PayoutLock /></div>
          <h3>Protect the payout</h3>
          <p>
            Once an account is eligible for a payout, the money stops being hypothetical — and
            that's exactly when accounts get blown. FixedR can pause trading on that account
            until you've taken the money out. Every other risk tool protects you from a loss;
            this one protects a win.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          {/* Echte Firmennamen (Michael-Entscheid 2026-08-27): eine Aussage über
              Anbindbarkeit, keine Partnerschaft und keine Empfehlung. */}
          <div class="chips">
            <span class="on">FTMO</span><span class="on">Apex</span><span>TopStep</span>
          </div>
          <h3>Pick the accounts</h3>
          <p>
            Send a trade to all your accounts, or to the ones you choose. Different firms,
            different platforms, one order ticket — sized correctly for each account rather
            than copied blindly.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="illu"><DynamicRisk /></div>
          <h3>Risk that follows a rule</h3>
          <p>
            One R doesn't have to be the same fraction forever. Let it follow the state of the
            account — smaller in drawdown, larger near target — written down as a rule in the
            account profile, not decided in the moment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Manifest-Teaser: die EINE dunkle Fläche der Seite. Die These ist kein weiterer
       Abschnitt, deshalb trägt die Farbe den Bruch. -->
  <section class="ink">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head center">
        <p class="eyebrow">The thesis</p>
        <h2>There is no money in a challenge account.</h2>
        <p>
          The balance of a funded account is notional — it isn't your money, and often not
          literal capital at all. What's real is your distance to the drawdown limit and to the
          target, both defined in percent. A currency display suggests a concreteness that
          doesn't exist. So we removed it.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:1.4rem"><a class="btn ghost" href="/manifesto">Read the manifesto</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Abschluss-CTA -->
  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head center" style="margin-bottom:0">
        <h2>Founders circle first.</h2>
        <p>
          FixedR is rolling out deliberately: a small group of prop traders first, then the
          waitlist, in order of signup.
        </p>
        <p style="margin-top:1.6rem"><a class="btn" href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
